# Programs the old compiler accepts that the new compiler compiles without an error but that are on neither pass
# list (tests\corpus\slice.list, tests\upstream\pass.list), each with the reason (spec testing/compiler-tests,
# "Clean programs are listed"; study\26 section 3). Shrink-only and kept by hand: tier 1 fails for a clean program on
# no list, and for an entry here that no longer compiles cleanly or that a pass list names.
corpus/runtime_comparison/126_print_comma.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/147_on_error_resume_0.bas  # loops forever by design: RESUME 0 re-runs ERROR 5 (KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/187_print_comma_zones.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/251_print_chain.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/80_print_semicolon.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
upstream/basic/val_default_large_integer_decimal.bas  # expects the VAL of libqb after 4.7.0: passes against the reference clone, fails against the 4.7.0 release CI uses, with qb64pe.exe of that release too (m2-core-builtins task 8.3)
upstream/basic/val_typed_large_integer_decimal.bas  # expects the VAL of libqb after 4.7.0: passes against the reference clone, fails against the 4.7.0 release CI uses, with qb64pe.exe of that release too (m2-core-builtins task 8.3)
